     "result_text_tail": "ough its service is still only proven outside the peak. An independent review of the recommendation raised this. The deck shows it as the main sensitivity, and the next steps ask the provider to confirm it in writing.\n\n**Choices I made because you weren't available:**\n- I used no data beyond the briefing pack and skipped the storyline approval step.\n- Closure is modeled from January 2027. The June close in the cost consultant's draft would halve the 2027 saving, which makes closure look worse.\n- Extra damage is held at $0.20M a year in 2028. If it grew with volume, the result would be slightly worse for closure.\n- One slide shows its figures in $ thousands ($100K, $750K, \u2212$650K), because the renderer rounded $0.75M to \"$0.8M\".\n\n**Checks:**\n- All 67 numbers are traced: 30 come straight from the pack and 37 are calculations with live formulas in the workbook. No placeholders are left.\n- The skill's QA checks pass with two warnings, both because the pack writes \"nine months\" and \"two-year\" in words.\n- The layout checks flagged no overflow. I couldn't look at the slides visually, because there's no LibreOffice here and the sandbox blocks opening Keynote. Please flick through the deck once in PowerPoint.\n\n**Next step:** I can switch to a different theme, or add a 2029 lease-renewal slide once East's renewal terms are known.\n\nFiles are in `deliverable/`:\n- `northline-east-dc.pptx`\n- `northline-east-dc-sources.xlsx`\n\nThe spec and build script are in `work/` if you want to re-render."
